:synohw_graphs_plug:
> **DX1215 level** (2026.10.25h): the level the module reads back after each DX evaluation (`@dx`), dashed: the level the daemon wanted (`@dxwant`), with the reason in the legend at the cursor; a red band where a fan alarm bit was set (`@dxal`). It is a separate chart because it is a level, not a percentage: no RPM or duty exists for the DX1215 fans (a 2-bit CPLD code).
>
> **Where the data comes from.** `/var/run/synology-hardware/history`, one line per evaluation (every 30 s, `CPU_PERIOD`), last 3000 lines (about 25 h), RAM only: it starts empty at every boot and is never written to the flash. Since 2026.10.25f each line also records the table mode, why the table chose its duty, the table duty itself, the sweep step during a fan sweep and every CPU sensor; older lines show "reason not recorded".
>
> **Which box a disk is in** is read from sysfs, never from the `sdX` name (which changes between boots): `/sys/block/<dev>/device` resolves through the PCI controller and the `ataN` port. Behind the Marvell 88SE9235 (`1b4b:9235`) or behind a port multiplier (`ataN/linkN.0` exists; the DX1215 uses Marvell 88SM9705, `1b4b:9705`) = **DX1215**; any other SATA controller = **DS2415+ internal**. The Source column says which path was found.
>
> **The dashed lines** are the steps of the table the daemon runs (`scemd.xml:17-29` LOW, `:3-15` HIGH; see the Fan table help): disk steps raise the fan to 40 / 70 / 99 %, disk alert in red; the CPU steps (65 / 85 &deg;C) are above the usual range, tick "Scale up to the CPU steps" to see them.
>
> **Fan duty** is what was sent to the MCU (`V<nn>`); the fan speed itself cannot be read (no tach). "Table duty" is what the table chose; the two differ only while a fan sweep holds the fan.
>
> **Library.** uPlot 1.6.32 (MIT, github.com/leeoniya/uPlot), shipped inside the plugin: the page loads nothing from the internet.
:end
